{"Title":"An Act to restore the effective date of MassHealth coverage for new applicants","BillNumber":"H1173","DocketNumber":"HD2440","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"G_C2","Name":"Gerard J. Cassidy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/G_C2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T13:06:00.687"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"G_C2","Name":"Gerard J. Cassidy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/G_C2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T13:06:00.6866667"},{"Id":"JBA1","Name":"Jennifer Balinsky Armini","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBA1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-01T14:57:09.7"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1173/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Cassidy of Brockton, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1173) of Gerard J. Cassidy and Jennifer Balinsky Armini relative to the effective date of MassHealth coverage for new applicants.  Health Care Financing.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 9A of chapter 118E of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting the following new paragraph:-\r\n\t(17) For applicants under age 65 who submit all required eligibility verifications within the time determined by the division, the start date of coverage shall begin on the first day of the third calendar month before the month of application.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J24","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}